body: |-
  ## What shipped

  ### Maestro Phases 1-5 (conductor-team-collab spec)
  - **P1**: Ambient context injection into agent profiles before spawning (decisions, journal, nominations via buildProfileEnrichment). Attribution prefix [nickname (role)] on every response. Symphony thr-orch-* thread recording.
  - **P2**: Conductor Swift — TeamThreadView (chat-style with colored roles, intent badges, diffs, decisions), AgentRosterView (active/benched with stats), SymphonyThreadWatcher (3s poll).
  - **P3**: AgentProfile.benched field. Orchestration + nomination engine skip benched agents. MCP paradigm_agent_bench/activate. CLI paradigm agent roster/bench/activate.
  - **P4**: Platform web Team section — TeamSection.tsx + teamStore.ts + routes/team.ts. Roster grid, thread viewer, bench toggle via REST.
  - **P5**: getNeverlandMetrics() — per-agent acceptance rates, thresholds, expertise, notebooks. Health classifier: cold-start → accumulating → calibrating → mature. paradigm_ambient_neverland MCP tool.

  ### Field Test Results (deus-backend)
  Opus ran a structured test modifying 7 files across auth, e2ee, moderation, DM features. Key findings:
  - Event pipeline works (14 events fired correctly)
  - Threshold adjustment works (builder 0.70→0.75, architect 0.50→0.55, security 0.40→0.45)
  - BUT nomination briefs are generic templates ("review for consistency")
  - Security at 0% accept rate despite auth/e2ee changes — blind to content
  - Flat scoring: all builders 0.7, all others 0.5
  - Self-silencing loop: bad briefs → dismissed → threshold rises → agent goes quiet

  ### Teacher Model (maestro-learning spec)
  Designed to fix the quality gap. Maestro as teacher, not just threshold adjuster:
  - **Session work log**: JSONL at .paradigm/events/session-log.jsonl captures agent contributions + user verdicts with reasons
  - **Postflight learning pass**: Maestro reads work log, writes targeted journal entries per agent (human_feedback for accepted, correction_received for dismissed)
  - **Documentor agent**: 6th core agent, always final orchestration stage, handles .purpose/portal.yaml/reindex via MCP only
  - **Stale expiry**: 7-day cutoff on pending nominations in stats
  - **autoPromote expanded**: human_feedback trigger now promoted to notebooks alongside pattern_discovered
  - **Guidance rewrite**: paradigm://guidance/orchestration fully documents Maestro model

  ## Architecture insight
  The learning pipeline (journal → notebook → buildProfileEnrichment) is also the mechanism for training agents with new behaviors. No separate "skill teaching" system needed — the pipeline IS the training mechanism. This only becomes visible once the learning loop produces quality entries, which is why the Teacher Model matters.
